:: Fishing Coast Path Approach Down
<<effects>>
<<silently>><<dancedifficulty 1 600>><</silently>>
<<if $rng gte 20 and !$danceSuccess>>
	You turn off the coastal path onto a narrow trail down the cliff face. The footing is uneven and it takes a bit of care, but you make it down without trouble.
<<else>>
	You turn off the coastal path onto a trail path down the cliff face. Your foot slips on a loose stone and you go down hard, <span class="red">scraping your hands and knees.</span>
	<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Coast Path Approach]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Approach
<<effects>>
An old wooden dock juts out below, half-rotten and creaking in the wind, it looks ready to collapse. You don't think it's safe to stand on the dock, but the path before it is safe enough.
<br><br>

<<if canStartFishing()>>
	<<fishingRodIcon>><<link [[Start fishing|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	If you had a fishing rod, you could probably catch fish from here
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Hike up the path (0:10)|Fishing Coast Path Approach Up]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Approach Up
<<effects>>
<<silently>><<dancedifficulty 1 600>><</silently>>
<<if $rng gte 20 and !$danceSuccess>>
	You head up the cliff trail to the coastal path.
<<else>>
	You head up the cliff trail. Halfway up, your foot slips and you go down on your hands, <span class="red">catching yourself before you slide back down.</span>
	<<gpain>><<pain 4>><<gstress>><<stress 3>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Coast Path]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>


/* The PC gets sent here any time they start fishing or after an event. From here, they get sent into the wait loop, where events can happen. */
:: Fishing Coast Path Wait
<<run initFishingCoastPath()>>
<<run startFishingProp()>>

<<fishingLocationDescription $bus>>
<<fishingLocationPopulation $bus>>
<br><br>

<<if $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<if isPregnancyEnding()>>
		<<pregnancyPassout "fishingCoastPath">>
	<<else>>
		<<passoutbeach>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $exposed gte 1>>
		<<exhibitionism "coastPathFishing">>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $arousal gte $arousalmax>>
		<<orgasmFishingCoastPath>>
	<<else>>
		<<fishingCoastPathWaitAmbient>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if fishingUsingMagnetRod()>>
		<<link [[Dredge for metal (0:05)|Fishing Coast Path Wait Loop]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Wait for a bite (0:05)|Fishing Coast Path Wait Loop]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Fishing Coast Path Approach]]>><<run stopFishingProp()>><</link>>
<</if>>
<<fishingCoastPathDebugLinks>>


/* Core fishing event loop. Sending the user here rolls for an event within the eventpool. */
:: Fishing Coast Path Wait Loop

<<cleareventpool>>
<<if fishingUsingMagnetRod()>>
	<<addinlineevent "magnetScrap" magnetLootWeight("fishingCoastPath", 1)>>
		<<set $fishingMagnetScrap to rollMagnetScrap("fishingCoastPath")>>
		<<include "Fishing Coast Path Magnet Scrap Catch">>
	<</addinlineevent>>

<<else>>
	<<addinlineevent "bite" fishingCatchEventWeight("fishingCoastPath", 8)>>
		<<set $fishingHookedFish to rollFish("fishingCoastPath")>>
		<<if fishingTriggersReelFight($fishingHookedFish)>>
			<<include "Fishing Coast Path Bite Big">>
		<<else>>
			You feel a tug on your line, then haul back on your rod, pulling <<a $fishingHookedFish.type>> out of the water without a fight.
			<<include "Fishing Coast Path Catch">>
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "trash" .2>>
		<<set $fishingTrash to rollFishingTrash("fishingCoastPath")>>
		<<include "Fishing Coast Path Trash Catch">>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "clothing" .2>>
		<<set $fishingClothingName to rollFishingClothing("fishingCoastPath")>>
		<<include "Fishing Coast Path Clothing Catch">>
	<</addinlineevent>>
<</if>>

/* Nothing happens, wait loop continues */
<<addinlineevent "wait" 25>>
	<<include "Fishing Coast Path Wait">>
<</addinlineevent>>
<<runeventpool>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Bite Big
<<effects>>
<<set $fishingReelAttempts to 0>>
The line goes taut and you lean out to look down into the water. You see <<if $fishingHookedFish.aboveAverageSize>>a <span class="pink">big</span> <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>><<else>><<a $fishingHookedFish.type>><</if>> trying to swim away, big enough to give you some trouble reeling it in.
<br><br>

<<set _reelDifficultyMax to Math.clamp($fishingHookedFish.size * 10, 600, 1400)>>
<<link [[Try to reel it in|Fishing Coast Path Reel]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty -250 _reelDifficultyMax>>
<br>
<<link [[Cut the line|Fishing Coast Path Cut Line]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Throw Back
<<effects>>
You toss the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> back into the surf.
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Keep
<<effects>>
You stow the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> away.
<<tending_give $fishingHookedFish.type 1>>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Cat Eat
<<effects>>
You open wide and drop the whole <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> in your mouth. <<transform cat 1>><<lstress>><<stress -6>>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Coast Path Wait Flavor [widget]
/* Text that is used to generally describe the PC waiting for a bite. Also includes the PC being alone with their thoughts, and descriptions of the PC noticing things around them, like the weather or noises around them that could signify that something dangerous about to happen. Also used to describe the player when they take an action other than waiting for a bite. */
<<widget "fishingCoastPathWaitAmbient">>
	<<cleareventpool>>
	<<fishingWaitAmbient $bus>>
	<<runeventpool>>
<</widget>>
